I have uploaded to /pub/Linux/Incoming a new version of the 
popuar pop-perl script for retrieving mail from a remote account.

I uploaded to /pup/Linux/Incoming, though I expect that it 
should go in the directory
   /pub/Linux/System/Mail/pop-perl5-1.1.tar.gz

This new version will work with Perl version 5, and it also has
some provision for using an alternate local delivery agent for 
mail rather than just appending downloaded mail to the user's 
mail spool file.  I use procmail for my local delivery agent.

I have not had any success in contacting either of the previous
authors/maintainers, and so I have slightly changed the name
of the files from pop-perl to pop-perl5 (since this is a version
specific to version 5 of Perl), and I bumped up the release
from 1.00 to 1.1

