NCD TO PROVIDE Z-MAIL FOR UNIX IN CALDERA'S NEW
NETWORK DESKTOP BUNDLE

Popular E-mail Package Provides Ideal Internet Access Solution to Linux Users

    NEW YORK, Sept. 19, 1995 -- NCD Software Corporation, a wholly owned
subsidiary of Network Computing Devices, Inc., (NASDAQ:NCDI) announced that its
Z-Mail for UNIX software package has been selected as the electronic mail
application in the new Network Desktop Bundle from Caldera, Inc.  Announced
today at the UNIX Expo tradeshow in New York, Caldera's new Network Desktop
Bundle will offer Linux users leading UNIX applications and is priced under
US$500.00.

    Z-Mail is an enterprise e-mail platform based on Internet protocols for
high scalability and reliability.  Z-Mail is designed for e-mail administrators
in large organizations, and includes complete cross-platform communication (for
Windows PCs, Macintosh computers, UNIX computers and character terminals),
standards-based interoperability, efficient message management, flexible
configuration, easy administration and low cost of ownership.

    "We believe that Z-Mail will be a key component to the bundle, as more and
more corporations look to electronic mail as their communication solution,"
said Barbara Tallent, director of marketing for Z-Mail products, NCD Software
Corporation.  "The fact that Z-Mail is cross-platform with easy access to the
Internet and World Wide Web only adds to the value of the bundle.  Because it
can be completely customized to any environment, Z-Mail is well suited for the
Linux platform."

    "Z-Mail is a valuable part of our new Network Desktop Bundle," said Ransom
Love, vice president of marketing and sales, Caldera, Inc.  "When we made the
decision to offer such a bundle to our customers, we set out to include only
the most innovative programs available to leverage the UNIX environment - Z-
Mail met and exceeded
our criteria."

    Caldera, Inc., a privately held company established in 1994, empowers the
Internet community, developers, OEMs, ISVs, industry partners, and end-users to
collaborate, innovate, build, and deliver meaningful computing alternatives to
the business community.

    NCD Software Corporation is a wholly owned subsidiary of Network Computing
Devices, Inc.  The company provides desktop information access solutions for
network computing environments.  NCD Software Corporation is a major supplier
of software products that include Mariner, an Internet access and navigation
tool that provides a unified interface to all Internet resources; PC-X server
software that integrates Microsoft Windows - and DOS-based PCs into X/UNIX
networks; and Z-Mail, a cross-platform electronic-mail and messaging system for
open systems environments.

