  Linux, a free Unix clone named from its developer, Linus Torvalds, is
  spreading rapidly through the unix community.  Adam Richter, President
  of Yggdrasil Computing in San Jose, will talk about Linux's origins
  and development, current Linux offerings including Yggdrasil's
  "Plug-and-Play" Linux, and ongong developments affecting Linux's future.
  
  Adam's talk will offer a comprehensive overview of Linux, aimed at
  current non-users.  It will not cover topics like installation and
  operational questions. If you've heard of Linux but know it sparsely,
  or are thinking about using Linux, this session is for you.
  
  Place:        Digital Equipment Corporation
                130 Lytton Street, Palo Alto CA
                (Corner of Alma, 1 block N. of University)
  
