		       Announcing genscript-1.1

Genscript is a free replacement for the enscript program.  Genscript
converts ASCII files to PostScript and spools generated PostScript
output to the specified printer or leaves it to file.  Genscript can
be easily extended to handle different output medias and it has many
options which can be used to customize printouts.

* News

  - bug and portability fixes
  - VMS multinational charset
  - cleanups in IBM PC and Mac charsets
  - new options:
    - -u, --underlay
    - -i, --indent
    - -D, --setpagecevice
    - -S, --statusdict
    - --page-label-format
  - AFM files are included in distribution
  - fixes in the ^@epsf escape
  - documentation fixes

* Features

  - support for following input encodings:
    - ISO-8859/1
    - IBM PC
    - 7 bit ascii
    - 7 bit ascii with some scandinavian extensions: {|}[\].
    - Macintosh 
    - VMS multinational
    - PostScript font's default encoding
  - support for AFM (Adobe Font Metrics) files
  - AFM files are included in distribution
  - output medias:
    - built-in medias: A4, A5, Letter, Legal
    - new medias can be added easily
  - special features:
    - inlined EPS images
    - change body font on-the-fly
    - pass key-value pairs to the statusdict and page device.  
      => duplex printing, papertray selection, etc.

* Available

  ftp://ftp.funet.fi/pub/unix/tools/genscript-1.1.4.tar.gz

  Genscript home page:	http://iki.fi/~mtr/genscript/
			(or http://www.hut.fi/~mtr/genscript/)

