The commercial acceptance and use of Linux continues to grow by leaps and
bounds:

UNIX EXPO:
----------
Unix Expo is the largest Unix oriented show in the US (33,000+ attendees),
and is held in late September every year at the Jacob Javits Convention
Center in New York City.

This year's show is being held Tuesday September 19th through Thursday
September 21st .

EXPO LINUX EXHIBITORS:
----------------------
Last year there were three exhibitors offering Linux based products or services:
The Linux Journal,  X Inside, and ACC's PC Unix and Linux Catalog.

This year's Unix Expo features more than twice that number and some -very-
impressive names. Some of companies exhibiting Linux products or services:

Caldera Inc.
Digital Equipment Company
Empress Software Inc.
Linux Journal
LXNY - The Linux Users Group of New York.
O'Reilly and Associates
Red Hat Software and ACC's PC Unix and Linux Catalog.

There will likely be other Linux vendors at the show who I am not currently
aware of so make sure you stop by either the LXNY booth #965, or the Linux
Journal's booth #2435 for a full list of vendors with Linux offerings at the
show.

LINUX EVENTS AT UNIX EXPO:
--------------------------
1.  LXNY will be hosting a Linux Users Group meeting on the evening of 
    Wednesday September 20th after the show at 5 pm in the downstairs
    meeting rooms 1E 18.
    The format will be a panel including 
    Matt Welsh - head of the LDP, and author of O'Reilly's bestseller
                Running Linux, 
    Michael K. Johnson - Editor of the Linux Journal,
    Erik Troan - Formerly the sunsite Linux archive adminstrator, and 
    Marc Ewing - Head of development of the Red Hat Commercial 
                Linux distribution.

2.  O'Reilly will be sponsoring a series of Seminars during the day on 
    Linux hosted by Matt Welsh.  You can find out more at any of: 
    O'Reilly's booth, or at the Linux Journal #2435 or LXNY #965.  
    Or try www.ora.com.

3.  Caldera Inc. will be showing the "Caldera Network Desktop" 
    an advanced desktop environment based on Linux.
    Their partners in this project who will be at the Expo include: Novell Inc.
    and Red Hat Software.  www.caldera.com

4.  Red Hat Software, at booth 966 will be demonstrating their Hot-Off-The-Press
    Red Hat 2.0 Commmercial Linux distribution.  It is being officially 
    released Tuesday morning at the show, and (unlike some vendors we know :)
    will also be shipping at that time.  www.redhat.com

